Here are 10 standard American English words, formatted with their meanings, real-world context, and natural pairings to help you build active vocabulary:\par
\par
Plausible\par
\par
Meaning: Seeming reasonable, believable, or likely to be true.\par
\par
Natural Pairing: "A plausible explanation" / "completely plausible"\par
\par
Example: "His story about missing the bus sounded plausible, so the teacher accepted it."\par
\par
Pragmatic\par
\par
Meaning: Dealing with things sensibly and realistically based on practical considerations rather than theories.\par
\par
Natural Pairing: "A pragmatic approach" / "take a pragmatic solution"\par
\par
Example: "Instead of arguing over ideal scenarios, they took a pragmatic approach to fix the immediate problem."\par
\par
Reluctant\par
\par
Meaning: Unwilling and hesitant to do something.\par
\par
Natural Pairing: "Reluctant to share" / "show reluctant agreement"\par
\par
Example: "She was reluctant to leave her hometown, but the new job opportunity was too good to pass up."\par
\par
Meticulous\par
\par
Meaning: Showing extreme care, thoroughness, and attention to detail.\par
\par
Natural Pairing: "Meticulous planning" / "meticulous attention to detail"\par
\par
Example: "The engineer paid meticulous attention to every line of code to prevent system bugs."\par
\par
Subtle\par
\par
Meaning: Delicate, precise, or so slight that it is difficult to analyze or describe directly.\par
\par
Natural Pairing: "A subtle difference" / "subtle hint"\par
\par
Example: "There was a subtle change in his tone that made me think he wasn't entirely convinced."\par
\par
Compelling\par
\par
Meaning: Evoking interest, attention, or admiration in a powerful and irresistible way.\par
\par
Natural Pairing: "A compelling argument" / "compelling evidence"\par
\par
Example: "The researcher presented compelling evidence that changed everyone's mind."\par
\par
Ambiguous\par
\par
Meaning: Open to more than one interpretation; not clear or explicit.\par
\par
Natural Pairing: "An ambiguous answer" / "remain ambiguous"\par
\par
Example: "His email was ambiguous, so I called him to clarify what he actually meant."\par
\par
Resilient\par
\par
Meaning: Able to withstand or recover quickly from difficult conditions or setbacks.\par
\par
Natural Pairing: "Remarkably resilient" / "build a resilient system"\par
\par
Example: "The team proved to be resilient, bouncing back stronger after their initial loss."\par
\par
Inevitable\par
\par
Meaning: Certain to happen; unavoidable.\par
\par
Natural Pairing: "An inevitable result" / "seem practically inevitable"\par
\par
Example: "With how fast technology evolves, change in the industry is inevitable."\par
\par
Discreet\par
\par
Meaning: Careful and circumspect in one's speech or action, especially to avoid causing offense or revealing private information.\par
\par
Natural Pairing: "Remain discreet" / "a discreet inquiry"\par
\par
Example: "Please be discreet about our plans until we make an official announcement next week."\par
